Deliverable acceptance (CON-ACC-03)

Issuer: Nivy Advisory s. r. o. · IČO 52 109 338 · Mlynské nivy 16, 821 09 Bratislava

The client has 10 business days to accept a deliverable or to reject it with written reasons tied to the agreed acceptance criteria.
Silence after the review window counts as acceptance where the statement of work says so; without that clause the Commercial Code rules on handover of the work apply instead.
A rejection buys one remediation cycle at no extra charge; further cycles are billed on time and materials.
Partial acceptance is recorded per criterion, so an open item does not block the whole milestone.
Final acceptance triggers the milestone invoice, payable within the contractual term, with statutory default interest running afterwards.
Handover includes the documentation and the source material the client needs to operate the result without the firm.

